# Citation File Format — https://citation-file-format.github.io/

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Gut-to-Pancreas Pathogen AMR Dashboard"
message: >-
  If you use this hackathon prototype or its pipeline outputs, please cite it
  and credit BV-BRC / CARD / NDARO / VFDB / PATRIC_VF / ESM2 as appropriate.
  Research prototype — not for clinical use.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Daytona Hackathon Team"
    website: "https://github.com/johnqh/daytona_hackathon"
repository-code: "https://github.com/johnqh/daytona_hackathon"
url: "https://github.com/johnqh/daytona_hackathon"
abstract: >-
  Pulls gut-derived pathogen AMR and virulence annotations from BV-BRC, embeds
  proteins with ESM2 on a Daytona H100, clusters them, generates grounded
  observations, and serves interactive CopilotKit dashboards. Measured negative
  finding: clusters do not separate resistant vs susceptible isolates.
keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - BV-BRC
  - Daytona
  - ESM2
  - CopilotKit
  - bioinformatics
  - hackathon
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-24"
